Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||01-14-2001||02:44 AM||||hi all! just got back from the hospital a while ago.. while removing the engine from my 87gt to install a clutch and do some other repairs, i had a jack collapse (lost hydraulic pressure) and in a roundabout way, forced a philips screwdriver through my hand (i have pics!) i think its gonna be a while to fix it now... but when i do, you can bet i will upload some burnout videos! seeya all later- gonna go ice up my hand. i got really luck, it went between the tendons/bones, and missed all the important bits, and hardly bled.. just gotta keep an eye out for infections. sorry for wasting your bandwidth with my rants!||||reg||1
